  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Yemen Joint Response 2024-2026 - Marib</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project will  contribute to local capacity building, particularly for local community committees, water management committees (WMCs),  and Community Health Volunteers (CHVs) in all stages of the project implementation, which can be effectively utilized in local emergency response in similar interventions. The project will also establish linkages between the local community structures with local authorities. For instance, WMCs will be connected with General Authority for Rural Water Supply (GARWSP) and National Water Resource Authority (NWRA) and will be responsible for the operation and maintenance of the rehabilitated water supply schemes, that will contribute to sustainability and adequate access of the target communities to safe drinking water. Likewise, CHVs will act as an integral community resource for promoting the adoption of good hygiene practices, will be connected with local health authorities and other organizations, and may refer communities to other service providers.</narrative>
  </description>
